---
// src/pages/bucknell/anop-400.astro  →  arizvi.com/bucknell/anop-400
// ANOP 400: how the term runs, where the clients come from, how it's graded, and what happens when it goes wrong. Not linked from the nav; sends noindex.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import CourseHeader from '../../components/CourseHeader.astro';
import CourseNav from '../../components/CourseNav.astro';
import Gantt from '../../components/Gantt.astro';
import HandedIn from '../../components/HandedIn.astro';
import { pack } from '../../data/packs/anop-400';
import { course } from '../../data/bucknell';

const c = course('anop-400');

// The ANOP 400 term, week by week.
const term = [
  { label: 'Scope', bars: [[1, 3]] as [number, number][] },
  { label: 'Data and discovery', bars: [[4, 6]] as [number, number][] },
  { label: 'Modelling', bars: [[7, 10]] as [number, number][] },
  { label: 'Recommendation', bars: [[11, 13]] as [number, number][] },
  { label: 'Delivery', bars: [[14, 14]] as [number, number][] },
  { label: 'With the client', marks: [{ w: 1 }, { w: 3 }, { w: 8 }, { w: 11 }, { w: 14 }] },
  { label: 'Team stand-ups', ticks: Array.from({ length: 13 }, (_, i) => i + 1) },
];

const brief = [
  ['The client', 'A regional credit union with 9 branches. Contact: the head of lending.'],
  ['The decision', 'Which members to call in the month before their car loan ends, so they refinance here.'],
  ['The data', '3 years of auto loans, about 40,000 rows. Member IDs replaced before the file reaches the team.'],
  ['The deliverable', 'A ranked call list for one month, and a 2-page memo on what a call is worth and where the cutoff sits.'],
  ['Success', 'A backtest on the last 6 months: how many of the members who refinanced elsewhere the list would have flagged in time.'],
  ['The client gives', '5 meetings (weeks 1, 3, 8, 11 and 14), 2 staff interviews in week 5, a 30-minute handover, a named contact, and the data by week 4.'],
];

---
<Base title="ANOP 400" description="ANOP 400, the Business Analytics Practicum, as Ali Rizvi would run it at Bucknell: the term, the clients, the grading, and what happens when a project goes wrong." noindex>
  <CourseHeader course={c} facts={[
    ['Format', '1 credit · 14 weeks · teams of 4 or 5, a client each'],
    ['What I\'d bring', 'A term planned to the week, a charter the client signs by week 3, a playbook for the week it goes wrong, and the habit of finding next term\'s clients during this one. The deliverable is a model and a recommendation the client can act on.'],
  ]}>
    <p>ANOP 400 has a client pipeline and an instructor who runs it, and I'd learn it before I touched it: sit in on a section in my first year, help where asked, and teach a section when the department asks. Below is how I'd run a section: the term, the clients, the grading, and what happens when a project goes wrong.</p>
    <p class="practice"><span class="label">From practice</span>A clinical trial is a capstone with higher stakes: the protocol is written before the first patient, the success measure is named in advance, and nobody moves it. The A/B tests I ran inside an e-commerce retailer worked the same way, with the metric and the stopping rule agreed before launch, and the ones that skipped that step produced quick wins that never showed up in revenue. The charter is that discipline, scaled to 14 weeks.</p>
  </CourseHeader>

  <Section label="The term" title="Week by week" id="term">
    <Gantt title="The ANOP 400 term, week by week" weeks={14} rows={term}
      caption="With the client: kick-off (week 1), signed charter (3), check-in (8), draft recommendation (11), final presentation (14). Every team gets a 15-minute stand-up with me each week, to week 13." />
  </Section>

  <Section label="Clients" title="Where the projects come from" id="clients">
    <div class="grid"><div class="span-8">
      <p>The course has a client pipeline already. If the department wants more clients than it has, this is where I'd look: businesses within an hour of campus, small businesses referred by the staff at Bucknell's SBDC, alumni-run companies, and regional non-profits with data they have never looked at. I'd start the term before, so every team has a client in week 1 and a signed charter by week 3. A company that AMJ Capital or I hold a stake in is never a client of a team I grade.</p>
      <p>Each client signs the 1-page charter and a data agreement with it, once the university has cleared the template: what the team gets, who may see it, and what the team may keep and show afterwards - the method and the memo with the numbers replaced, unless the client agrees to more. Customer and member IDs are replaced before a file reaches students, and students sign an NDA where the client asks for one.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="grid" style="margin-top: 2rem;"><div class="span-8">
      <p class="label">A sample brief · fictional</p>
      <div class="kv brief">
        {brief.map(([k, v]) => (<><p class="label">{k}</p><p>{v}</p></>))}
      </div>
    </div></div>
  </Section>

  
  
  <HandedIn pack={pack} />

  <Section label="When it goes wrong" title="The playbook" id="playbook">
    <div class="grid"><div class="span-8">
      <ol>
        <li><strong>The client hasn't signed by week 3.</strong> The charter is marked on the team's draft, and the team starts on the plan B dataset while I chase the signature.</li>
        <li><strong>The client goes quiet.</strong> It happens, and usually around week 9. The charter names a plan B dataset in the same domain, and the team switches at that week's stand-up without losing the week.</li>
        <li><strong>The data is late.</strong> The week 4 deadline is in the charter. The team starts on a public stand-in the same day, and the client's file replaces it when it lands.</li>
        <li><strong>A teammate disappears.</strong> Stand-up records and the week 7 peer evaluation make it visible early. I have the conversation in week 7, and the grade follows the record.</li>
        <li><strong>The client changes the question.</strong> The charter is re-signed, and the report keeps the week 3 version as what changed and why.</li>
        <li><strong>The model says nothing useful.</strong> That is a finding. The memo says what the data can and cannot support, and what to collect next year.</li>
        <li><strong>The client can't make week 14.</strong> The presentation goes ahead with me in the client's chair, the client gets the recording and the report, and the 45% is unchanged.</li>
      </ol>
    </div></div>
  </Section>

  <CourseNav current={c.slug} />
</Base>
